# GitHub Personal Access Token (classic)
#
# Required for build-time GitHub stats on the /about page:
#  - Contribution calendar (heatmap)
#  - Pinned repositories
#  - Language breakdown
#  - Follower / following counts
#
# Without this token, the about page falls back to mock data.
#
# How to create one:
#   1. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   2. Click "Generate new token (classic)"
#   3. Give it a name (e.g. "ricki-web build")
#   4. No scopes needed — the GraphQL API returns public data without
#      any selected scopes.  (Selecting `read:user` or `repo` also works.)
#   5. Copy the generated token here.
#
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# WakaTime API Key
#
# Required for build-time WakaTime coding stats on the /dashboard page:
#  - Total coding time this week
#  - Daily average
#  - Best day
#  - Language breakdown with progress bars
#
# Without this key the dashboard still renders — WakaTime sections show
# a placeholder ("set WAKATIME_API_KEY in your deploy environment").
#
# How to get one:
#   1. Sign in at https://wakatime.com
#   2. Go to Settings → API Key
#   3. Copy your secret API key here.
#   4. Also enable "Make my data public" in Settings → Privacy if you want
#      the /users/current endpoint to work without extra scopes.
#
WAKATIME_API_KEY=

# Anthropic API Key (server-side only)
#
# Required ONLY for the generative RAG answer on the /ask page.
# The endpoint /api/ask runs as a Vercel serverless function and calls Claude
# to write a cited answer over content retrieved client-side.
#
# Without this key the site still deploys and /ask works — it just shows the
# ranked semantic results (source excerpts + links) without a generated answer.
#
# Set it in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment Variables),
# NOT in the client. It is never exposed to the browser.
#
#   1. Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#   2. Add ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in Vercel (or your .env for local `astro dev`).
#
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
